<h3>Why WHtR is useful</h3>

Waist-to-height ratio is a straightforward screening measure for central
body fat. A commonly cited guideline is to keep your waist under half your
height.

<h3>How it is calculated</h3>

Waist circumference divided by height, both in the same units. Bands
differ between men and women, and this calculator applies the appropriate
set.
